{"name":"Sugar Tree","hex":"#a2999a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sugar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food consisting of small, sweet crystals, principally of sucrose, obtained from sugar cane or sugar beet and used as sweetener and preservative.","Any specific variety of sugar."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add sugar to; to sweeten with sugar.","To make (something unpleasant) seem less so."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sugar"},{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Acer saccharum","blocks":[{"text":"Acer saccharum, the sugar maple, is a species of flowering plant in the soapberry and lychee family, Sapindaceae. It may also be called rock maple, sugar tree, sweet maple, or, particularly in reference to the wood, hard maple."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg/330px-Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acer_saccharum"},{"title":"Sugar","blocks":[{"text":"Sugar is a class of sweet-tasting, soluble carbohydrates, many of which are used in food. Simple sugars, also called monosaccharides, include glucose, fructose and galactose. Compound sugars, also called disaccharides or double sugars, are molecules made of two bonded monosaccharides; common examples are sucrose, lactose and maltose. White sugar is almost pure sucrose. During digestion, compound sugars are hydrolysed into simple sugars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg/330px-Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugar"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg/500px-Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg/1280px-Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg/500px-Acer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_%285098070608%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAcer_saccharum_1-jgreenlee_(5098070608).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Acer_saccharum_seeds.jpg/330px-Acer_saccharum_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co